---
layout: sitePage.liquid
permalink: /offline/index.html
mainClass: offline
eleventyComputed:
  title: '{{ "interface:offlineTitle" | t | strip_html }}'
  crumb: '{{ "interface:offline" | t | strip_html }}'
---
<article>
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>
  <h2>SuttaCentral</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a
        class="with-icon"
        href="{{ scOrigin }}/offline"
        rel="external"
      >
        {% icon "devicePhoneMobile" %}
        <span>Web app (PWA)</span>
      </a>
      <p>
        Install SuttaCentral.net as an app and keep the texts you choose for
        reading offline. Needs JavaScript and an up to date browser, and can be
        unreliable to install.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a class="with-icon" href="/editions">
        {% icon "bookOpen" %}
        <span>Editions</span>
      </a>
      <p>
        Whole books of translations, as ePub, PDF or HTML files, or in print.
      </p>
    </li>
  </ul>
  {% if _siteMetaData.archive %}
    <h2 id="scx-offline">{{ _siteMetaData.title }}</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a class="with-icon" href="{{ _siteMetaData.archive }}">
          {% icon "archiveBoxArrowDown" %}
          <span>Site archive</span>
        </a>
        <p>
          The whole site as plain HTML files to download, which work on any
          computer or smartphone with a local web server.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="with-icon" href="{{ _siteMetaData.archive }}">
          {% icon "computerDesktop" %}
          <span>Native apps</span>
        </a>
        <p>
          The whole site as an app to install on macOS, Windows, Linux or
          Android, which opens like any other.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="with-icon" href="{{ _siteMetaData.archive }}">
          {% icon "documentArrowDown" %}
          <span>Kiwix ZIM</span>
        </a>
        <p>
          The whole site as one file for
          <a href="https://kiwix.org" rel="external">Kiwix</a>, the free offline
          reader for phones, tablets and computers.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  {% endif %}
</article>
